able solution. 2.1 r1 3(b)(i) states the value of the game for summer. 1.1b b1 value of the game for summer = 4 3(b)(ii) states the play-safe strategy for each player. 1.1b b1 play safe strategy for summer: s3 play safe strategy for haf: h2 total 5","73662d-nov20-04":"4 the connected planar graph p is eulerian and has at least one vertex of degree x. some of the properties of p are shown in the table below. number of vertices number of edges number of faces 3x + 6 x2 + 8x 2x2 + 2 deduce the value of x. fully justify your answer. [4 marks] q marking instructions ao marks typical solution 4 uses euler’s formula for connected planar graphs (pi). 3.1a m1 as the graph is planar and connected then v – e + f = 2 3x + 6 – (x2 + 8x) + 2x2 + 2 = 2 x 2 – 5x + 6 = 0 x = 3 or x = 2 however, an eulerian graph cannot have a vertex of degree 3 therefore x = 2 forms a correct unsimplified equation in x using euler’s formula. 1.1a m1 solves quadratic equation and gives two solutions (cao). 1.1b a1 deduces that x = 2 by completing a reasoned argument that only even values of x are valid because p is an eulerian graph. (ft their odd and even values of x) 2.2a r1f total 4","73662d-nov20-05":"5 a restoration project is divided into a number of activities. the duration and predecessor(s) of each activity are shown in the table below. activity immediate predecessor(s) duration (weeks) a – 10 b – 5 c b 12 d a 8 e c, d 4 f c, d 3 g c, d 7 h e, f 8 i g 6 j g 15 k h, i 5 l k 4 5 (a) on the opposite page, construct an activity network for the project and fill in the earliest start time and latest finish time for each activity. [4 marks] key activity earliest start time latest finish time duration 5 (b) due to a change of materials during the project, the duration of activity c is extended by 3 weeks. determine the new minimum completion time of the project. [2 marks] q marking instructions ao marks typical solution 5(a) constructs an activity network with activities a to g drawn with correct ar