) recognises limitation of rectangular distribution in modelling situation with reference to the shape of the histogram 3.5b e1 the frequency density on the histogram is not approximately level between 8 and 12 hours use the normal distribution instead refines the model by suggesting the use of the normal distribution 3.5c b1 total 2 question total 4 paper total 50","73673s-jun23-01":"1 the discrete random variable a takes only the values 0, 2 and 4, and has cumulative distribution function f(a) = p(a − a) a 0 2 4 f(a) 0.2 0.6 1 find p(a = 2) circle your answer. [1 mark] 0 0.4 0.6 0.8 q marking instructions ao marks typical solution 1 circles correct answer 1.1b b1 0.4 question total 1","73673s-jun23-02":"2 the time, t days, between rain showers in a city in autumn can be modelled by an exponential distribution with mean 1.25 find the distribution of the number of rain showers per day in the city. tick (3) one box. [1 mark] distribution mean exponential 0.8 exponential 1.25 poisson 0.8 poisson 1.25 q marking instructions ao marks typical solution 2 ticks correct answer 1.1b b1 poisson, mean 0.8 question total 1","73673s-jun23-03":"3 the masses of tins of a particular brand of spaghetti are normally distributed with mean m grams and standard deviation 4.1 grams. a random sample of 11 tins of spaghetti has a mean mass of 401.8 grams. construct a 98% confidence interval for m, giving your values to one decimal place. [3 marks] q marking instructions ao marks typical solution 3 obtains correct z-value awrt 2.33 condone 2.32 pi by a correct upper or lower limit of the confidence interval 1.1b b1 z = 2.33  4.1 401.8 2.33 11 = (398.9, 404.7) uses formula for upper or lower limit of a confidence interval using their z-value or t-value. condone use of 4.1 pi 1.1a m1 obtains correct confidence interval awrt 1 d.p. condone use of truncated z-value of 2.32 1.1b a1 question total 3","73673s-jun23-04":"4 the random variable x has a normal distribution with unknown mean m and un