d change if a sample of size 5 was taken with the same mean and standard deviation. [1 mark] q marking instructions ao marks typical solution 3(a) obtains correct z value. awrt 1.88 pi by a correct upper or lower limit of the confidence interval. 1.1b b1 z = 1.88 = = (1188.5, 1203.5) uses formula for upper or lower limit of a confidence interval using their z-value and sample mean and variance. condone use of may use t-value. 1.1a m1 obtains correct confidence interval awrt 1dp. 1.1b a1 2s x z n ± ± 98 1196 1.88 600 98 3(b) states yes and explains that the sample size has changed and is part of the calculation or a t distribution would be used instead of a z distribution or the confidence interval will be wider. 2.4 e1 yes as the sample size has changed and is part of the calculation. total 4","73673s-nov20-04":"4 the discrete random variable x follows a discrete uniform distribution and takes values 1, 2, 3, …, n. the discrete random variable y is defined by y = 2x 4 (a) using the standard results for x n, x n2 and var(ax + b) , prove that var(y ) = n2 × 1 3 [7 marks] 4 (b) a spinning toy can land on one of four values: 2, 4, 6 or 8 using a discrete uniform distribution, find the probability that the next value the toy lands on is greater than 2 [1 mark] 4 (c) state an assumption that is required for the discrete uniform distribution used in part (b) to be valid. [1 mark] q marking instructions ao marks typical solution 4(a) uses formula for e(x) 1.1a m1 e(x) = = = e(x 2) = = = var (x) = = = = var (y) = var (2x) = 22 var (x) = 4 × = obtains an expression for e(x) by using the formula for 1.1b a1 uses formula for e(x 2) 1.1a m1 obtains an expression for e(x 2) by using the formula for 1.1b a1 uses the formula for var (x) or uses var (y) = 22 var (x) 1.1a m1 obtains correct expression for var (x) 1.1b a1 completes a rigorous algebraic proof by using var (y) = 22 var (x) to show that var (y) = 2.1 r1 ... n i x n n n = + + + = ∑ 1 1 2 ( ) n n n + 1 2 n +1 2 ... n i x n