 introduced a new law changing d to 2 before the government introduced the new law, the probability that a water pipe is given a ‘red’ rating was 0.05 6 (a) explain whether or not the probability that a water pipe is given a ‘red’ rating has increased as a result of the new law. [4 marks] 6 (b) find the probability density function of the random variable x. [2 marks] 6 (c) after investigation, the distances between successive breaks in water pipes are found to have a standard deviation of 5 metres. explain whether or not the use of an exponential model in parts (a) and (b) is appropriate. [2 marks] q marking instructions ao marks typical solution 6(a) uses the mean equalling 25 to find the value of λ 3.3 m1 λ = 0.04 p(x ≤ 2) = 1 – e-0.04 × 2 = 0.077 > 0.05 the probability of a ‘red’ rating has increased. evaluates an exponential model to find p(x ≤ 2) or uses it to find x 3.4 m1 find p(x ≤ 2) = awrt 0.077 or x = awrt 1.3 metres. 1.1b a1 concludes probability higher or probability will be increased because 2 metres is higher than 1.3 metres. ft ‘their’ probability or x value. 3.2a e1f λ = 1 25 6(b) states the correct probability density function for x ≥ 0 for their value of λ 1.1b b1f states the complete correct probability density function including x < 0 (or otherwise). 1.2 b1f . . ( ) x x e f x − ≥   =    0 04 0 0 04 otherwise 0 6(c) obtains the standard deviation of the expon","73673s-nov20-07":"7 the rainfall per day in february in a particular town has been recorded as having a mean of 1.8 inches. sienna claims that rainfall in february has increased in the town. she records the rainfall in a random sample of 12 days. her sample mean is 2 inches and her sample standard deviation is 0.4 inches. it is assumed that rainfall per day has a normal distribution. 7 (a) investigate sienna’s claim using the 5% level of significance. [6 marks] 7 (b) for the test carried out in part (a), state in context the meaning of a type ii error. [1 mark] 7 (c) the distribution 